String trim()
Returns the copy of the String, by removing whitespaces at both ends. Whitespace characters between words remain unchanged.
public class Geeks {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "   Hello, Trim!   ";
        System.out.println("'" + s.trim() + "'");
    }
}
'Hello, Trim!'
